"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a phase one budget of $500,000 and a kick-off on June 15th. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate to leverage AI research. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions scheduled for September 10th. Key milestones include a call for R&D ideas by July 20th to enhance data visualization, the completion of the testing phase celebrated on October 10th, and the transition to the development phase led by Omar Jensen. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
